  "claim": "Successor of the frozen presentation of COPRIME-DICHOTOMY-20261027-001D: a self-contained presentation (presentation.md) of the counting dichotomy for G = N x| C_r (N of exponent p and class c < p, r | p - 1) on closed 3-manifolds with H1(M; F_p) = 0 and boundedly many sectors, corrected after the independent AI review of COPRIME-DICHOTOMY-20261027-001: the pair condition supplies a compatible parity automorphism (the action need not factor through C2); the literal Fox matrix of the closure relators is t^-1 (Bur_t - I); the cable homomorphism uses the integer abelianization exponent; the edge weight is used with its actual coefficients. It expands the canonical pinned coordinates and the reading-strand construction with its basis proof (COPRIME-PAIRS-20261027-001A), gives precise references, and records every review as independent AI review with finite V2 checks, not human expert or formal certification. Frozen predecessors are unchanged (hashes checked). Pair failures in classes 3 and 4 remain open there.",
